Error [E1119]: `align(3)` is not a usable layout alignment.
  --> tests/ui/layout_alignment_invalid.jet:1:18
    |
  1 | #Layout(c, align(3))
    |                  ^
 Why: `#Layout(c, align(N))` requires a positive power-of-two supported by the selected target profile and the portable baseline; `#Layout(c, align(target, N))` uses the selected target profile without the extra portable baseline; the value is not a power of two.
 Fix: Write `#Layout(c, align(2))` with a positive power-of-two supported by the selected profile, or use `align(target, N)` only with a profile fact that proves the larger boundary.
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E1119
